Markdown Coding Style Manifesto
================================

> Strict layout regulations and presentation aesthetics enforced across corporate documentation.

&nbsp;

This document defines the layout rules governing documentation within this ecosystem. All AI engines (LLMs) or engineers expanding documentation MUST preserve these rules to eliminate cognitive friction and ensure formatting consistency.

&nbsp;
&nbsp;


________________________________________________________________________________

## 1. Title Formatting

Main titles MUST utilize the Setext style format, underlined completely by equal signs extending across the entire title string length. Do not use ATX style headers (#) for the primary module title.

```markdown
My Package Title
================
```

&nbsp;
&nbsp;


________________________________________________________________________________

## 2. Executive Summaries

Every Markdown document MUST immediately supply a brief, punchy structural overview or executive pitch wrapped inside a native blockquote syntax element (">").

```markdown
> Structured error classification and thread-safe logging utilities for corporate applications.
```

&nbsp;
&nbsp;


________________________________________________________________________________

## 3. Section Boundary Spacing (Vertical Pacing Rules)

To ensure absolute visual predictability across terminal previews, code editor viewports, and raw HTML render tools, blocks of information MUST be padded using explicit white-space and non-breaking space markers ("&nbsp;").

The termination of sections dictates the formatting layout structure for what follows next:

### Level 2 Sections (##)
When finishing any H2 section block, you MUST inject exactly 2 blank lines, 2 lines with "&nbsp;", 2 more blank lines, and exactly one 80-character horizontal rule before starting the next heading.

```markdown
Last paragraph of H2 section content.


&nbsp;
&nbsp;


________________________________________________________________________________

## Next H2 Section Heading
```

### Level 3 Sections (###)
When finishing any H3 section block, you MUST inject exactly 2 blank lines, 1 line with "&nbsp;", and 2 more blank lines before starting the next heading.

```markdown
Last paragraph of H3 section content.


&nbsp;


### Next H3 Section Heading
```

### Level 4 Sections (####)
When finishing any H4 section block, you MUST inject exactly 1 blank line, 1 line with "&nbsp;", and 1 more blank line before starting the next heading.

```markdown
Last paragraph of H4 section content.

&nbsp;

#### Next H4 Section Heading
```

### Deep Levels (##### and ######)
To maintain structural cohesion without bloating vertical scroll distance, Level 5 and Level 6 subsections do not use "&nbsp;" anchors. Separate them using exactly 2 native blank lines above them, and 1 blank line below them.

```markdown
Last paragraph of H5/H6 section content.


##### Next H5 Section Heading
```
